":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"15a1c38fbff299939f9abdef3d2ad8ecf8908233f0c2ac826d0e5649eef9b71a","event_uuid":"29f1cab2-4663-4bb1-8e4a-7d2be6fa4a8e","position":{"commit_sha":"a7c03e72c404acd783df0572b4b310f8b3133075","position":"1788604262161557001-29f1cab2-4663-4bb1-8e4a-7d2be6fa4a8e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"70409b0e1404e22ad463d47f9772f030eaeed0ad4fb195e58feb6f33a5b1df0d","event_uuid":"ca30ad92-2036-407f-ae88-d53b3a195c82","position":{"commit_sha":"f9c5987355ee4c48bb1bb35866cf9674c8093c6b","position":"1788608048841919001-ca30ad92-2036-407f-ae88-d53b3a195c82"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Additional advisory from c6ce plan-review re-attestation (non-blocking): the corroborator hand-rolls process-group termination (_terminate: killpg SIGTERM -> 1s grace -> killpg SIGKILL -> wait) instead of delegating to rebar._proc.reap_process_group, the harness's named single source of truth for reaping a timed-out grounding child + its group (bug d843). Consider delegating to reap_process_group when addressing the subprocess-memory-bound item, since both touch _run's subprocess lifecycle.","timestamp":1788604262161557001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Additional minor cleanup surfaced while certifying the REB-640 epic: leaf 08ab's description still contains an AC verify-command referencing the pre-rename ADR path 'test -f docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md' (the terraform ADR actually landed at 0115). 08ab's file_impact was corrected to 0115, but the AC verify-command prose in its description was left as-is (advisory only; the completion gate does not execute it, and 08ab's original close passed with the file already at 0115). Cosmetic doc-consistency fix for a future pass.","timestamp":1788608048841919001}],"created_at":1788602441866463001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e5e22f16-beea-4d97-9778-d201a99eb2ee","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c6ce-4d8d-1c12-47cc"}],"description":"Follow-up advisories from Gerrit change 2672 (c6ce) patchset-2 LLM-Review (PASS, non-blocking). Captured here so they are not lost after the corroborator lands.\n\n1. (correctness) Bound PEAK MEMORY of the terraform-config-inspect subprocess. src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py:_run — proc.communicate(timeout=...) buffers the childs ENTIRE stdout/stderr into memory before the len(stdout) > MAX_STDOUT / MAX_STDERR check runs, so a runaway or hostile binary can OOM the host before the post-hoc cap is enforced. The 60s deadline bounds time but not memory. Fix: read both pipes incrementally under the deadline and abort (abstain worker_failure) once a running total exceeds the cap, instead of a post-communicate() length check. Threat is primarily a buggy/runaway legitimate binary on a large module (a malicious same-named binary on PATH already implies code-exec as the user).\n\n2. (maintainability) Dead filter clause in _minimal_env: `if k in _KEEP_ENV and not _drop_env(k)`. _KEEP_ENV is a closed allowlist (LANG, LC_ALL, LC_CTYPE, SYSTEMROOT, WINDIR, COMSPEC, PATHEXT) and none of its members match any _DROP_ENV_PREFIX, so `and not _drop_env(k)` is always True. Remove the dead conjunct (or add a comment justifying defence-in-depth) so the filter is not misleading.\n\n3. (tests) Strengthen non-disclosure on the MATCH path. tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py::test_exact_declaration_matches_every_supported_class drives the corroborator with _module_json() whose variable description and default are both SECRET, but never asserts SECRET is absent from evidence+receipt on the positive match path (other abstain-path tests do). Add the assertion so the digest-only redaction is pinned on the match path too.\n\nAcceptance criteria: all three addressed with tests; corroborator suite + terraform seam suites green; no new LLM-Review blocking findings.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","a374-849c-c8f2-4234"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ca1f-88ee-6211-4bff","ticket_type":"task","title":"Corroborator PS2 advisories: bound subprocess memory, dead env filter, match-path non-disclosure test","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["25f84f29-48ad-4448-8882-6e07935357ac","5fa93e09-cb7c-4a9c-90b9-899191aae50b","e5e22f16-beea-4d97-9778-d201a99eb2ee","29f1cab2-4663-4bb1-8e4a-7d2be6fa4a8e","ca30ad92-2036-407f-ae88-d53b3a195c82"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788610764192346719,"uuid":"65307ccc-abec-4a26-8bf0-aef83f0c8029"}